# Google Workspace Docs / Sheets

## When to use

User asked to find, read, comment on, or edit a Google Doc or Spreadsheet
(including tabs, tables, ranges, formatting). Prefer a connected Google
Workspace MCP.

## MCP tool map — Docs

Pass `user_google_email` as the connected MCP documents (example pattern:
`admin@nodadyoushutup.com`). Never invent document ids.

| Job | Tools |
| --- | --- |
| Search docs | `search_docs` (`query`) |
| List docs in folder | `list_docs_in_folder` (optional `folder_id`) |
| Plain text | `get_doc_content` (`document_id`) |
| Markdown + comments | `get_doc_as_markdown` (`document_id`, comment opts) |
| Structure / indices | `inspect_doc_structure` (`document_id`) — **required**
  before index-based inserts |
| Create | `create_doc` (`title`, optional `content`) |
| Safe text swap | `find_and_replace_doc` (no index math) |
| Targeted text / style | `modify_doc_text`, `update_paragraph_style` |
| Headers / footers | `update_doc_headers_footers` |
| Batch ops | `batch_update_doc` (`operations`; prefer
  `end_of_segment=true` when appending) |
| Tables | `create_table_with_data` (index from
  `inspect_doc_structure.total_length`); `debug_table_structure` |
| Images / elements | `insert_doc_image`, `insert_doc_elements` |
| Tabs | `manage_doc_tab` |
| Comments | `list_document_comments`, `manage_document_comment` |
| Export PDF | `export_doc_to_pdf` (`document_id`, optional folder) |

## MCP tool map — Sheets

Never invent spreadsheet ids. Name the tab and A1 `range_name` on writes.

| Job | Tools |
| --- | --- |
| List spreadsheets | `list_spreadsheets` |
| Sheet metadata | `get_spreadsheet_info` (`spreadsheet_id`) |
| Read values | `read_sheet_values` (`spreadsheet_id`, optional
  `range_name`, formulas/notes/hyperlinks flags) |
| Write / clear values | `modify_sheet_values` (`range_name`, `values` or
  `clear_values=true`) |
| Format range | `format_sheet_range` |
| Conditional format | `manage_conditional_formatting` |
| Structured tables | `list_sheet_tables` → `append_table_rows` |
| Create workbook / tab | `create_spreadsheet`, `create_sheet` |
| Rows / columns | `resize_sheet_dimensions` (insert/hide/delete/
  freeze/auto-resize) |
| Move rows | `move_sheet_rows` |
| Comments | `list_spreadsheet_comments`, `manage_spreadsheet_comment` |

Creates, writes, clears, deletes, and PDF export need an explicit verb when
destructive or content-changing beyond an authorized edit — see
`google-workspace-safety`.

## Procedure

1. **Resolve id** — `search_docs` / `list_spreadsheets` / `list_docs_in_folder`
   (or Drive search) before inventing ids. **Done when** `document_id` /
   `spreadsheet_id` is from MCP.
2. **Read first** — Docs: prefer `get_doc_as_markdown` or `get_doc_content`;
   call `inspect_doc_structure` before any index-based insert. Sheets:
   `get_spreadsheet_info` then `read_sheet_values` for the target range.
   **Done when** you know structure and the range/section to touch.
3. **Edit smallest** — Docs: prefer `find_and_replace_doc` or scoped
   `modify_doc_text` over full rewrite; append via batch with
   `end_of_segment`. Sheets: write only the named A1 range; never clear a
   sheet unless asked.
   **Done when** MCP confirms the edit and unrelated cells/sections stay
   intact.
4. **Tables** — Docs tables: inspect → create/populate →
   `debug_table_structure` if wrong. Sheets tables: `list_sheet_tables` before
   `append_table_rows`.
   **Done when** table shape matches the data.
5. **Evidence** — return title, id, tab/range or section touched, and what
   changed. **Done when** no unauthorized wipe/delete/export ran.

## Defaults

1. Never invent document, spreadsheet, tab, or table ids.
2. Prefer section / range edits over full-document or full-sheet rewrites.
3. Sheets: always name tab + A1 range on write; do not overwrite unrelated
   cells.
4. Preserve existing structure unless asked to reformat.
5. Export to PDF only when requested.
6. Do not paste secrets into shared docs or cells.
7. Neighbor desktop office formats are out of scope except via Drive import
   helpers when the user asked.

## Refuse

- Do not delete tabs, wipe sheets (`clear_values` on large ranges), or drop
  rows/columns without an explicit ask (`google-workspace-safety`).
- Do not skip `inspect_doc_structure` when using index-based Doc inserts.
